                        "translation_id": "7089c4a3-91b2-4e7b-b70a-29a1960e253a",
                        "source_entry_id": "db73d5c7-91b8-3b35-a11d-602df6a5e698",
                        "source_sense_id": "970821db-08d5-3d94-8a52-b1f257f7d17a",
                        "target_lang_word": "Ruscism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Ruscism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ff614473-4498-3c33-a27e-6d544bfdf916",
                                        "entry_id": "383ab056-1f48-3e2a-87d6-6a657eeeb4f7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Russian fascism, Russianism, Great Russian chauvinism; the ideology of Russia, seen as fascism or as fascist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "neologism",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "815458f3-08ae-4ea8-9a3c-e069925266a1",
                                                "sense_id": "ff614473-4498-3c33-a27e-6d544bfdf916",
                                                "text": "Pro-Ukrainian commentators also used the word Rashizm. Derived from Rasha (from the English “Russia”), combined with the Russian fashizm, and perhaps best translated as “Ruscism,” this term is . . ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c019a18-8549-4a9e-addf-15bd60c21d6d",
                                                "sense_id": "ff614473-4498-3c33-a27e-6d544bfdf916",
                                                "text": "Pro-Ukrainian commentators have also used the word ‘Rashism’ (conflation of ‘Russia’ and ‘fascism’) to emphasize the aggressive intentions of Russia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f1b4dbf-ad3c-4dcb-aad2-d3bbb0e2c447",
                                                "sense_id": "ff614473-4498-3c33-a27e-6d544bfdf916",
                                                "text": "On the other side, a large segment of the Ukrainian press has been presenting the Putin regime as fascist: commentators have coined the nickname Putler (Putin + Hitler) and the term Rashism, which conflates Russia and fascism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "712d6bff-3836-47b2-93f8-d6b2ecf00d5f",
                                                "sense_id": "ff614473-4498-3c33-a27e-6d544bfdf916",
                                                "text": "[…] science, and science-based ultramodern technologies (AI) invented for progress have transformed into cynical means of conducting the third world war by immoral intellect of the ideologists of Ruscism [4]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8b5d622-f4c6-415c-8c97-683dd62fe6f3",
                                                "sense_id": "ff614473-4498-3c33-a27e-6d544bfdf916",
                                                "text": "“We have beat fascism, and we will defeat Ruscism,” said Pavel Kirilenko, governor of the Donetsk region, who arrived with heavily armed guards to lay flowers at the monument."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
